      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "North Face revolutionized climbing cinematography. Unlike the distant shots in <a href=\"/movie/20187\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"20187\">The Eiger Sanction</a> (1975), Stölzl put cameras directly on the face, capturing the vertigo-inducing exposure that would influence later films like Dawn Wall (2017). The sound design - creaking ice, labored breathing, wind - creates suffocating tension similar to <a href=\"/movie/49047\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"49047\">Gravity</a> (2013), proving you don't need space to convey isolation."
      }
